# REGRESSION PIN — indirect-call `&`-param ABI, TYPE axis cell: **8-byte
# non-resource struct** (`struct{int}`), through an ANNOTATED LOCAL `Callable`.
# This is the original repro of the defect the R43 Track C write-site fix
# retired; its test is LIVE (not `#[ignore]`d) and asserts the intended output.
#
# THE DEFECT IT PINS: at an indirect call each argument's pointer-vs-value ABI
# was GUESSED from the ARGUMENT's pointee shape at two independent backend read
# sites, instead of being WRITTEN from the CALLEE's declared parameter
# ownership. The guess coincides with the truth for scalars and for
# resource-containing aggregates and DIVERGES for a non-resource aggregate
# behind a `&` — so the call site passed the struct BY VALUE into a callee (and
# an `__adapt_*` shim) declared to take a pointer.
#
# RED-VERIFIED against the PRE-fix compiler (`git checkout -- src && cargo build`,
# then re-run — reverting a patch does NOT rebuild the binary):
#     gg check              -> rc 0, "OK: no semantic errors"
#     C    -> builds rc 0, binary rc 139 (SIGSEGV), no output
#     LLVM -> builds rc 0, binary rc 139 (SIGSEGV), no output
# POST-fix both backends print `2`.
#
# ⚠ THE 2x2 THAT FIRST FRAMED THIS DEFECT WAS TOO NARROW — recorded so the
# narrowing is not re-derived. It read "LOCAL + struct& breaks, LOCAL + int& and
# PARAM + struct& work". Measured across the full type axis, the LOCAL binding
# was broken for EVERY non-resource aggregate (struct 8B/16B/40B, mixed
# register classes, nested structs, `Option[int]`), and the surviving green
# cells (`int`, `float`, `bool`, `String`, `Vector`, `Dict`, `struct{String}`)
# were green only ACCIDENTALLY — they are pinned as such in
# callable_amp_abi_scalar_cells.gg and callable_amp_abi_resource_cells.gg.
#
# LANE AXIS (self-host driver, `--emit-c` -> cc -> run): rc 139. The self-host
# has its OWN indirect-call ABI defect (it never forms the pointer at all) and
# is 0/13 across this net's type cells; filed in TODO.md.
#
# WHY IT STAYS IN known_gaps/: `runtime_parity_corpus` reads only
# `tests/fixtures/*.gg` and never descends subdirectories, so the LIVE test
# asserts on C AND LLVM with ZERO self-host parity-corpus inflow. Graduating it
# to the top level while the SH lane still fails it WOULD be new parity debt.
#
# INTENDED: prints `2` on both backends — the callee writes through the `&`.
struct P:
    int n

void bump(P &p):
    p.n = p.n + 1

int main():
    Callable[void(P &)] f = bump
    P p = P(1)
    f(&p)
    print(p.n)
    return 0
